{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790459023,"nonce":"FIdtYlzVR7puBm7ygRmBcvRa0Es=","title":"Plugins export their members under caribou::link's symbols, for AOT linking","message":"For the static linking chosen for AOT (ash 9b3753c, 0683393), a plugin's\nmember is called directly by the symbol caribou::link names for it,\nwith the rule's C signature. A plugin's classes are already C functions\nwith typed signatures (caribou_abi's plugin! macro and caribou-bindgen's\ngenerated table), so the macro exports each member under that symbol as\nwell, and a plugin built as a static library or a wasm side module is\nlinkable by name. The dynamic path (the plugin table the loader reads)\nstays for hosted runs.","files":null}]}